#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# region_member

#% text
# `region_member(reg, p)` tells whether the point `p` lies in the region `reg`: `true` or `false` for a numeric point, a condition for a symbolic one.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Boundaries belong to closed regions.

#% item
# `region_member(reg, [p1, p2, ...])` answers for several points.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A point of the unit disk:

#% cell
region_member(disk(), [1/2, 1/2])
#% output
#= true

#% text
# A symbolic point gives the condition:

#% cell
region_member(disk(), [x, y])
#% output
#= element(x | y, reals) and x^2 + y^2 <= 1

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Several points of a polygon:

#% cell
region_member(polygon([[0, 0], [2, 0], [2, 2], [0, 2]]), [[1, 1], [3, 3], [2, 1]])
#% output
#= [true, false, true]

#% text
# A box:

#% cell
region_member(cuboid([0, 0, 0], [1, 2, 3]), [1/2, 1, 4])
#% output
#= false

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `region_distance`, `implicit_region`
